    description: "Single sweep PR mechanically retrofitting analyzers that already call `make_unresolved_edge` with a clear `module_hint` argument. The change is one-line per call site: add `dst_ref=ExternalRef(lang=..., module_path=module_hint, name=callee_name)` alongside the existing `module_hint=` kwarg.\n\nThese analyzers don't need language-specific import-resolution logic — they already know the module at the emit site (typically because they emit during import-declaration walks rather than call-expression walks).\n\nTarget candidates (initial sketch — verify with `git grep \"make_unresolved_edge\"` before authoring):\n- `requirements.py` — Python `requirements.txt` lines have explicit module names.\n- `cmake.py` — `find_package(X)` / `include(X)` have module = X.\n- `py_deps.py` — pyproject.toml dependency edges.\n- `jvm_deps.py` — Gradle / Maven dependency edges.\n- `manifest_targets.py` — build manifest cross-refs.\n- Any analyzer where `git grep \"make_unresolved_edge\" <file>` shows module_hint != \"external\" and the callee name is structured.\n\nNON-target (excluded):\n- The 7 already-retrofitted analyzers from PR2 (java, go, elixir, js_ts, cpp, rust, ruby).\n- Python's py.py — already retrofitted in PR1.\n- Analyzers that emit `make_unresolved_edge` with `module_hint=\"external\"` (the literal sentinel) — these have no module info to attach to dst_ref, so the retrofit is a no-op.\n- Analyzers using ad-hoc `Edge.create(dst=f\"…\")` instead of `make_unresolved_edge` — those need per-analyzer audit, not a sweep.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Each retrofitted analyzer's tests stay green.\n- New unit test (parametric) verifies `dst_ref is not None` on emitted unresolved edges for at least one fixture per retrofitted analyzer.\n- No SCHEMA bump needed (dst_ref already in schema as of PR1's 0.7.1 → 0.7.2 patch).\n\nTrigger: after WI-kaziv (bakeoff validation) confirms Phase 1's value. If the bakeoff signal is muted, this sweep is still safe to do — it's purely additive — but lower priority.\n\nEstimate: probably <30 min per analyzer × 5-8 analyzers = <4 hours total. Could be a single PR."  # 80cc
    fields: {}  # 80cc
